msgid "# KV Trace"
msgstr "# KV Trace"

msgid ""
"KV Trace is an opt-in diagnostic for investigating KV-cache address-plan errors\n"
"in Ascend Model Runner V2 (MRV2). It compares native scheduler declarations with\n"
"the final slot mappings, block tables and sequence lengths used by the runner,\n"
"once per KV cache group. It is disabled by default."
msgstr ""
"KV Trace 是按需启用的诊断能力，用于排查昇腾 Model Runner V2（MRV2）中的 KV cache 地址计划错误。它按 KV "
"cache group 比较原生调度声明与 runner 最终使用的槽位映射、块表和序列长度，默认关闭。"

msgid ""
"Use it when you need to check whether a request's scheduled token range and KV\n"
"block bindings agree with the runner's final address metadata. An in-range\n"
"address can still belong to the wrong token or request; KV Trace checks the\n"
"exact destinations as well as capacity."
msgstr ""
"KV Trace 用于核对请求的调度 token 范围和 KV 块绑定，检查它们与 runner "
"最终地址元数据是否一致。即使地址在合法范围内，也可能指向了错误的 token 或请求；KV Trace 同时检查精确目的地址和容量边界。"

msgid "## Requirements and Limitations"
msgstr "## 使用前提与限制"

msgid ""
"- Use a vLLM/vLLM Ascend combination that includes KV Trace, with MRV2 enabled.\n"
"- Adapted dense paged-attention (PA) and multi-head latent-attention (MLA) paths\n"
"  use one final metadata view per cache group in eager and FULL modes. Allocator\n"
"  and kernel block coordinates must match. Hardware qualification currently\n"
"  covers dense TP1/PP1 generation; qualify MLA and multi-rank deployments\n"
"  separately.\n"
"- Configuration checks raise an error for CP, DBO, speculative decoding,\n"
"  encoder/decoder models and cache layouts beyond ordinary append-only\n"
"  addressing. These modes require their own address rules.\n"
"- Trace evidence covers worker-local request bindings and final address plans.\n"
"  Block lifetime, initialized prefixes, KV values and transfer integrity require\n"
"  separate observations. Prefix sharing and reuse of the same physical block ID\n"
"  can produce the same worker messages.\n"
"- Historical fixed-workload measurements showed at most 0.66% throughput\n"
"  decrease with normal INFO logging. See the performance section for the tested\n"
"  revision, workload and first-token latency."
msgstr ""
"- 使用包含 KV Trace 的 vLLM/vLLM Ascend 版本组合，并启用 MRV2。\n"
"- 已适配的稠密分页注意力（PA）和多头潜在注意力（MLA）路径在 eager、FULL 模式下，每个 KV cache group 使用一份最终元数据视图。分配器与内核的块坐标必须一致。当前硬件验证覆盖稠密模型 TP1/PP1 生成；MLA 和多 rank 部署需要分别验证。\n"
"- 配置检查会对 CP、DBO、投机解码、编码器/解码器模型，以及普通追加式地址布局之外的缓存布局报错。这些模式需要各自的地址规则。\n"
"- 追踪记录覆盖 worker 本地请求绑定和最终地址计划。块生命周期、已初始化前缀、KV 数值以及传输完整性需要单独取证。前缀共享与同一物理块 ID 的复用，可能产生相同的 worker 消息。\n"
"- 历史版本的固定负载实测中，计入普通 INFO 日志后，吞吐下降最高约 0.66%。验证版本、负载和首 token 延迟见性能章节。"

msgid "## Usage"
msgstr "## 使用方法"

msgid "### Configuration"
msgstr "### 配置"

msgid "| `kv_trace` option | Type | Default | Meaning |"
msgstr "| `kv_trace` 选项 | 类型 | 默认值 | 含义 |"

msgid ""
"| `enabled` | bool | `false` | Enable the MRV2 observer for this engine. |"
msgstr "| `enabled` | bool | `false` | 为当前引擎启用 MRV2 观测。 |"

msgid ""
"| `action` | `\"log\"` or `\"raise\"` | `\"log\"` | Log violations or stop "
"returning model results. |"
msgstr "| `action` | `\"log\"` 或 `\"raise\"` | `\"log\"` | 记录异常，或阻止模型结果正常返回。 |"

msgid ""
"Omitting `kv_trace` or setting `enabled=false` disables the observer. Accepted\n"
"keys are `enabled` and `action`; their types and values follow the table above.\n"
"Configure the feature through `additional_config.kv_trace`, and select MRV2 with\n"
"`VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER`."
msgstr ""
"省略 `kv_trace` 或设置 `enabled=false` 会关闭观测。配置接受 `enabled` 和 `action` "
"两个键，类型与取值按上表填写。通过 `additional_config.kv_trace` 配置此能力，并用 "
"`VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER` 选择 MRV2。"

msgid "### Online Serving"
msgstr "### 在线服务"

msgid ""
"Replace `/path/to/model` with a supported dense model and retain your deployment's\n"
"other required options. The following example enables logging in FULL mode.\n"
"Set the runner selection before starting the service:"
msgstr ""
"将 `/path/to/model` 替换为已支持的稠密模型路径，并保留部署所需的其他参数。以下示例在 FULL 模式下启用日志记录。请在启动服务前设置"
" runner 选择："

msgid ""
"`tee` saves standard output and standard error to `kv-trace-server.log` in the\n"
"current directory. KV Trace writes to the vLLM process logger; `tee` creates\n"
"and saves the log file."
msgstr ""
"`tee` 将标准输出和标准错误保存到当前目录的 `kv-trace-server.log`。KV Trace 向 vLLM 进程日志输出记录，由 "
"`tee` 创建并保存日志文件。"

msgid ""
"For eager execution, replace `--compilation-config ...` with `--enforce-eager`.\n"
"To stop normal output after a violation, change `action` to `raise` and restart\n"
"the service. A `raise` failure can terminate EngineCore and require a complete\n"
"engine restart."
msgstr ""
"使用 eager 模式时，将 `--compilation-config ...` 替换为 `--enforce-"
"eager`。如需在发现异常后停止交付结果，将 `action` 改为 `raise` 并重启服务。`raise` 异常可能终止 "
"EngineCore，需要重启整个引擎。"

msgid "### Offline Inference"
msgstr "### 离线推理"

msgid "Select MRV2 in the environment before starting the Python process:"
msgstr "在启动 Python 进程之前，通过环境变量选择 MRV2："

msgid "## Log Output and Analysis"
msgstr "## 日志输出与分析"

msgid "### Log Records"
msgstr "### 日志记录"

msgid "Records go through the vLLM logger to the process log:"
msgstr "记录通过 vLLM logger 输出到进程日志："

msgid ""
"- `kv_trace.enabled`: the configured failure action.\n"
"- `kv_trace.bind`: reconstructed request bindings, token ranges and native finish/preempt notices.\n"
"- `kv_trace.write` / `kv_trace.read`: per-group final execution plans.\n"
"- `kv_trace.boundary`: native update or connector public input/result fields.\n"
"- `kv_trace.violation`: an address-plan constraint violation and its expected/actual fields."
msgstr ""
"- `kv_trace.enabled`：配置的异常处理方式。\n"
"- `kv_trace.bind`：重建的请求绑定、token 范围以及原生完成/抢占通知。\n"
"- `kv_trace.write` / `kv_trace.read`：每个 group 的最终执行计划。\n"
"- `kv_trace.boundary`：原生更新返回结果或 connector 的公开输入/输出字段。\n"
"- `kv_trace.violation`：地址计划约束异常及其期望值/实际值。"

msgid ""
"`log` records violations and continues. `raise` latches the first violation\n"
"and stops normal result delivery; the exception can terminate EngineCore.\n"
"An audit can complete after native execution has submitted device writes; those\n"
"writes remain in place. Observation gaps produce DEBUG-level `check skipped`\n"
"records. Only `kv_trace.violation` latches a failure."
msgstr ""
"`log` 记录异常并继续执行。`raise` 锁存首次异常并停止交付结果，异常可能终止 "
"EngineCore。审计完成时，原生执行可能已经提交设备写入，这些写入会保留。观测缺失会输出 DEBUG 级别的 `check skipped` "
"记录。只有 `kv_trace.violation` 会锁存失败状态。"

msgid "### Address Checks"
msgstr "### 地址检查"

msgid ""
"The expected addresses come from each step's native request bindings and\n"
"computed/scheduled token ranges. KV Trace compares them with the final metadata\n"
"in the runner's actual batch order."
msgstr ""
"期望地址由每一步的原生请求绑定以及已计算/已调度 token 范围推导。KV Trace 按 runner 实际 batch "
"顺序，将这些地址与最终元数据比较。"

msgid "| Constraint | Example |"
msgstr "| 约束 | 示例 |"

msgid ""
"| Exact token destination | Cross-request slot swaps, shifted writes or "
"writes into the padded tail. |"
msgstr "| 精确 token 目的地址 | 跨请求槽位交换、写入偏移或写入填充尾部。 |"

msgid ""
"| Logical block order | The input read table differs from the declared "
"request binding. |"
msgstr "| 逻辑块顺序 | 输入读表与声明的请求绑定存在差异。 |"

msgid ""
"| Declared length | The final input length differs from the scheduled token "
"range. |"
msgstr "| 声明长度 | 最终输入长度与调度 token 范围存在差异。 |"

msgid ""
"| Capacity and reserved storage | A write exceeds cache capacity or violates"
" the configured null-block reservation. |"
msgstr "| 容量与保留存储 | 写入超出缓存容量，或违反当前配置的 null-block 保留规则。 |"

msgid ""
"| Dummy writes | A dummy write target violates the PAD/native null-block "
"rules. |"
msgstr "| Dummy 写入 | Dummy 写入目标超出 PAD/原生 null-block 规则允许的范围。 |"

msgid ""
"Warmup/capture scratch belongs to synthetic execution. Ordinary dummy writes\n"
"use PAD `-1`; native block tables can explicitly enable null-block redirection."
msgstr "预热和图捕获的临时数据属于合成执行。普通 dummy 写入使用 PAD `-1`；原生块表可以显式启用 null-block 重定向。"

msgid "### Observation Boundaries"
msgstr "### 观测边界"

msgid ""
"Bindings record native new/resumed replacements and cached block appends.\n"
"Finished/preempted notices remove worker-local request references. Verify\n"
"physical block release separately through allocator-side evidence."
msgstr ""
"绑定记录新请求/恢复请求的原生替换，以及已缓存块的增量追加。完成/抢占通知会移除 worker 本地请求引用。物理块释放需要通过分配器侧证据单独确认。"

msgid ""
"Read/write records describe the final metadata after native execution. In\n"
"async TP1/PP1 generation, the audit can finish during result retrieval or before\n"
"the next metadata observation. Other result paths use synchronous checking.\n"
"Each audit uses the request bindings saved for its own step."
msgstr ""
"read/write 记录描述原生执行后的最终元数据。异步 TP1/PP1 "
"生成中，审计可以在获取结果时或下一次元数据观测前完成。其他结果路径采用同步检查。每次审计使用对应步骤保存的请求绑定。"

msgid ""
"Zero/copy fields record the native `update_requests` return boundary. Confirm\n"
"content readiness separately. Connector records retain public input fields and\n"
"the native finished/failed/invalid result sets. A receive can appear in both\n"
"the finished and failed sets, so inspect those fields together. Submission\n"
"identity and remote-content validity require separate connector evidence."
msgstr ""
"Zero/copy 字段记录原生 `update_requests` 的返回边界，内容就绪状态需要单独确认。connector "
"记录保留公开输入字段及原生完成/失败/无效结果集合。一次接收可以同时出现在完成和失败集合中，排查时应合并查看这些字段。提交身份和远端内容有效性需要单独的"
" connector 证据。"

msgid "## Troubleshooting"
msgstr "## 故障排查"

msgid "### Find the Violation"
msgstr "### 查找异常记录"

msgid ""
"Use the saved process log from the online example. The following example came\n"
"from controlled fault injection with `action=raise`."
msgstr "使用在线服务示例保存的进程日志。以下示例来自使用 `action=raise` 的受控故障注入。"

msgid ""
"In a controlled read-table fault run on Ascend 910B4 at revision\n"
"`11ba7b73079bda403be5c795f1d6d9c1a43045d4`, Qwen3-0.6B BF16 with MRV2 FULL,\n"
"TP1/PP1 returned HTTP 500 with this client error:"
msgstr ""
"在版本 `11ba7b73079bda403be5c795f1d6d9c1a43045d4` 的 Ascend 910B4 "
"受控读表故障验证中，Qwen3-0.6B BF16 使用 MRV2 FULL、TP1/PP1，客户端收到 HTTP 500 和以下错误："

msgid ""
"The service then exited, and a subsequent health request reported\n"
"`ConnectionError`. Use the server's violation and exception records to identify\n"
"the cause of an HTTP 500. Search the saved log:"
msgstr ""
"随后服务退出，后续健康检查报告 `ConnectionError`。结合服务端的异常记录和异常栈，定位 HTTP 500 的原因。请检索已保存的日志："

msgid ""
"The same run produced the following records. Timestamps, log levels and source\n"
"locations are omitted; process IDs and event fields are retained:"
msgstr "同一次运行产生了以下记录。为便于阅读，省略了时间戳、日志级别和源码位置，保留进程 ID 和事件字段："

msgid ""
"Here group 0 expected the logical block order `[1, 2, 3, 4]` but observed\n"
"`[2, 1, 3, 4]`. The first two block IDs were swapped. All IDs can be within\n"
"capacity while the read plan targets the wrong blocks. This record establishes\n"
"an address-plan mismatch. KV values and physical allocation behavior require\n"
"separate verification."
msgstr ""
"此处 group 0 的期望逻辑块顺序为 `[1, 2, 3, 4]`，实际记录为 `[2, 1, 3, 4]`，前两个块 ID 被交换。即使所有 ID"
" 都在容量范围内，读计划仍可能指向错误的块。这条记录确认了地址计划差异。KV 数值和物理分配行为需要单独验证。"

msgid "### Identify the Affected Request"
msgstr "### 关联受影响的请求"

msgid ""
"Request and step correlation uses the surrounding trace records. In this\n"
"single-request example, the following `kv_trace.read` record from the same\n"
"EngineCore identifies the request. Use the process and request IDs from your\n"
"own log:"
msgstr ""
"请求和步骤的关联依赖上下文记录。这个单请求示例中，同一个 EngineCore 随后的 `kv_trace.read` 记录给出了请求 "
"ID。请使用你自己的日志中的进程 ID 和请求 ID："

msgid ""
"For concurrent requests, use the actual `request_ids` row order with the\n"
"expected/actual table rows and retain the surrounding records. An async audit\n"
"can follow a later `kv_trace.bind`, so the nearest bind may describe a later\n"
"step. For ambiguous request or step attribution, report the candidate records\n"
"and the remaining uncertainty."
msgstr ""
"并发请求应结合实际 `request_ids` 的行顺序与期望/实际块表各行分析，并保留上下文。异步审计可能排在后续 `kv_trace.bind` "
"之后，最近的一条 bind 可能描述后续步骤。请求或步骤归属存在歧义时，请一并提供候选记录和待确认事项。"

msgid "### Restart and Verify Recovery"
msgstr "### 重启并确认恢复"

msgid ""
"In `raise` mode the failure remains latched and can stop the complete service.\n"
"Preserve the log before restarting:"
msgstr "`raise` 模式下，失败状态会持续锁存，可能导致整个服务停止。重启前先保存日志："

msgid ""
"Remove any test fault-injection hook before retrying. For an unexpected failure,\n"
"retain the model, software revisions, launch options, triggering workload and\n"
"full log for diagnosis. Restart the complete engine/service through your normal\n"
"process manager after the old process exits, preserving the original model,\n"
"execution settings and failure action. When retrying a `raise` failure, keep\n"
"`action=raise` in the launch command above. Start a fresh engine with a fresh\n"
"KV cache. The `action` setting controls the response to a violation; recovery\n"
"requires investigating and correcting the address mismatch."
msgstr ""
"重试前移除测试故障注入 "
"hook。遇到非预期故障，保留模型、软件版本、启动参数、触发负载和完整日志，用于诊断。旧进程退出后，通过正常的进程管理方式重启整个引擎/服务，保留原有模型、执行设置和异常处理方式。重试"
" `raise` 故障时，上述启动命令应继续使用 `action=raise`。使用新引擎重新建立 KV cache。`action` "
"控制发现异常后的处理方式；恢复服务还需要调查并修正地址差异。"

msgid "In another terminal, check readiness and retry a small request:"
msgstr "在另一个终端中检查服务就绪状态，再重试一个小请求："

msgid ""
"Confirm recovery using three results: health HTTP 200, completion HTTP 200 with\n"
"generated text, and zero new violations for the retry. In the fresh server log,\n"
"check `kv_trace.enabled` and the `kv_trace.write` / `kv_trace.read` records for\n"
"that retry. The final `grep` reports trace and exception records; check readiness\n"
"and request results through the two HTTP responses. The archived evidence\n"
"covers detection and service exit. Validate the restart procedure in your\n"
"deployment."
msgstr ""
"结合三项结果确认恢复：健康检查返回 HTTP 200，生成请求返回 HTTP 200 和生成文本，且该次重试的新增异常数为 0。在新的服务端日志中，检查"
" `kv_trace.enabled` 以及该次重试的 `kv_trace.write` / `kv_trace.read` 记录。最后一条 "
"`grep` 用于查找追踪和异常记录，服务就绪状态和请求结果应分别查看两次 HTTP "
"响应。归档证据覆盖异常检测和服务退出，重启流程请在自己的部署中验证。"

msgid "## Validation and Performance"
msgstr "## 验证与性能"

msgid "### Functional Validation"
msgstr "### 功能验证"

msgid ""
"At revision\n"
"[`11ba7b73079b`](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/commit/11ba7b73079bda403be5c795f1d6d9c1a43045d4),\n"
"[service validation](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/43542402730/attempts/2)\n"
"passed both eager and FULL cases, comparing tracing OFF/ON for sequential and\n"
"concurrent generation with prefix caching and chunked prefill."
msgstr ""
"版本 [`11ba7b73079b`](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-"
"ascend/commit/11ba7b73079bda403be5c795f1d6d9c1a43045d4)的[服务验证](https://github.com/vllm-"
"project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/43542402730/attempts/2)中，eager 和 FULL "
"两项用例均通过，比较了启用前缀缓存、分块预填充时，追踪 OFF/ON 下的串行与并发生成结果。"

msgid ""
"A separate 2026-11-14 Ascend 910B4 run used the same revision's Python feature\n"
"sources, vLLM `24420b7a341af37a9bc3186e6fc6062512e0aa58`, and native extensions\n"
"and custom OPP from a v0.30.0 image. With Qwen3-0.6B BF16, MRV2, TP1/PP1:"
msgstr ""
"2026-11-14 的另一轮 Ascend 910B4 验证使用同一版本的 Python 特性源码、vLLM "
"`24420b7a341af37a9bc3186e6fc6062512e0aa58`，以及 v0.30.0 镜像中的原生扩展和 custom "
"OPP。模型为 Qwen3-0.6B BF16，使用 MRV2、TP1/PP1："

msgid ""
"- 32 complete healthy requests passed across eager/FULL and tracing OFF/ON,\n"
"  covering sequential, four-way concurrent and streaming generation, plus\n"
"  retries after client stream cancellation. Four intentionally cancelled\n"
"  streams are counted separately. Paired text/stream outputs matched and each\n"
"  healthy engine recorded 2,688 prefix-cache hit tokens.\n"
"- Eight controlled write-slot/read-table fault requests produced the expected\n"
"  violations: four `log` requests returned HTTP 200; four `raise` requests\n"
"  returned HTTP 500 and the service exited. The final two FULL read-table cases\n"
"  also recorded the native graph-replay call and return."
msgstr ""
"- 在 eager/FULL 与追踪 OFF/ON 的组合下，32 个完整正常请求通过，覆盖串行、4 路并发、流式生成及客户端中断流后的重试。另有 4 次主动中断的流单独计数。配对的文本/流式输出一致，每个正常引擎均记录了 2,688 个前缀缓存命中 token。\n"
"- 8 个受控写槽位/读块表故障请求均产生预期异常：4 个 `log` 请求返回 HTTP 200；4 个 `raise` 请求返回 HTTP 500，随后服务退出。最后两项 FULL 读表用例还记录了原生图回放的调用与返回。"

msgid ""
"These results cover controlled address-plan faults. Production incidents,\n"
"performance, MLA, multi-rank TP/PP, Mooncake network transfer, preemption and\n"
"long-term stability each require separate validation."
msgstr "这些结果覆盖受控地址计划故障。生产故障、性能、MLA、多卡 TP/PP、Mooncake 网络传输、抢占和长期稳定性，需要各自的专项验证。"

msgid "### Historical Performance Measurements"
msgstr "### 历史性能测量"

msgid ""
"Performance measurements belong to revision\n"
"[`2883638529ac`](https://github.com/Tjh-UKN/vllm-ascend/commit/2883638529ac02c9ee1ef29a41a8158da9d0782a),\n"
"before the package rename and CI follow-ups. Repeat the benchmark when\n"
"evaluating later revisions, including `11ba7b73079b`."
msgstr ""
"性能数据来自版本 [`2883638529ac`](https://github.com/Tjh-UKN/vllm-"
"ascend/commit/2883638529ac02c9ee1ef29a41a8158da9d0782a)，测量时间早于包目录重命名和 CI "
"后续修改。评估后续版本（包括 `11ba7b73079b`）的性能时，请重新运行基准测试。"

msgid ""
"The run used Ascend 910B4, Llama-3.1-8B BF16, MRV2 FULL, TP1/PP1, input/output\n"
"lengths 2048/256, prefix caching disabled and normal INFO trace logging enabled.\n"
"Eight fresh engines, four OFF and four ON, completed all 520 requests across\n"
"16 formal windows, each longer than 60 seconds."
msgstr ""
"该轮使用 Ascend 910B4、Llama-3.1-8B BF16、MRV2 FULL、TP1/PP1，输入/输出长度为 "
"2048/256，关闭前缀缓存，并计入普通 INFO 追踪日志开销。8 个新启动的引擎（4 个 OFF、4 个 ON）在 16 个正式窗口中完成了全部 "
"520 个请求，每个窗口均超过 60 秒。"

msgid "| Concurrency | Throughput decrease | TTFT increase |"
msgstr "| 并发数 | 吞吐下降 | TTFT 增幅 |"

msgid ""
"TTFT is time to first token. Treat the -0.11% throughput change as measurement\n"
"variation. Results apply to this revision and workload; repeat the benchmark\n"
"for later revisions. CPU/RSS cost requires separate measurement."
msgstr ""
"TTFT 表示首 token 延迟。-0.11% 的吞吐变化按测量波动看待。结果适用于该版本和负载，后续版本的性能需重新测量。CPU/RSS "
"开销需要单独测量。"
